# Packages to take from a given feed when several feeds carry them, as
# <feed>/<package>. Installed before anything else: otherwise the first feed
# whose package depends on one installs it from the earliest feed in
# feeds.conf.
#
# Currently EMPTY, and that is deliberate.
#
# This used to pin luci_smstool/sms-tool (4IceG's 2026-08 build) so that
# byte/files/etc/rc.local and luci-app-modeminfo had a /usr/bin/sms_tool to
# shell out to. QModem now owns the modem stack and ships sms-tool_q as a
# separate package installing /usr/bin/sms_tool_q, so every caller was moved
# to that binary and the un-suffixed package is no longer selected
# (build/config: CONFIG_PACKAGE_sms-tool is not set). Keeping the pin would
# install a second, unused SMS tool into the image.
#
# The luci_smstool feed itself stays in build/feeds - feeds.prefer and
# feeds.exclude are read independently, and removing the feed would change
# every feed index for no gain.
